# Privacy Policy — NewsOnCompose

**Last updated:** November 25, 2025

NewsOnCompose ("we", "our", or "us") operates the NewsOnCompose mobile application (the "App"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect information when you use the App or visit our privacy page.

If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or want to exercise your rights, contact us at: **EMAIL@YOURDOMAIN.COM**.

---

## 1. Information We Collect

### 1.1 Personal Information
We may collect personal information you provide directly, for example:
- **Email address** — if you sign up, subscribe, or contact us.
- **Name** — only if you choose to provide it.

### 1.2 Usage & Device Information
We automatically collect certain information about your device and usage, including:
- Device model, OS version, app version.
- IP address (briefly, for analytics and rate-limiting).
- Log data and crash reports.
- Usage data (pages viewed, searches, time spent) to improve the App.

### 1.3 Saved & Offline Content
If you save articles for offline reading, we store that content locally on your device. We may also cache article metadata to improve performance.

### 1.4 Analytics & Cookies (Website)
If you visit our privacy page on the web, we may use cookies and similar technologies to analyze usage. Cookies are not required to use the App.

---

## 2. How We Use Information

We use the collected information to:
- Provide, maintain, and improve the App.
- Personalize content and improve user experience.
- Diagnose and fix technical issues and crashes.
- Send communications about updates or important information (only with your consent where required).
- Comply with legal obligations.

---

## 3. Third-Party Services

We may use third-party services that collect, process, or store data on our behalf, such as:
- **Analytics providers** (e.g., Firebase Analytics) to understand app usage.
- **Crash reporting** (e.g., Crashlytics) to collect crash logs and fix bugs.
- **Image loading libraries** (e.g., Coil) which may cache remote images locally.

If we integrate advertising or additional third-party SDKs in the future (e.g., ad networks), those providers may collect information according to their own privacy policies. We will update this policy when we add or change third-party services.

---

## 4. Data Retention

We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to provide the App and for legitimate business purposes (e.g., analytics, bug fixes), or as required by law. Usage and aggregated data may be retained longer in anonymized form.

---

## 5. Legal Bases for Processing (If EU/GDPR applies)

If you are in the EEA, our legal bases for processing personal data include:
- Processing necessary for performance of a contract with you.
- Our legitimate interests (improving and securing the App).
- Your consent, when required (e.g., certain communications).

---

## 6. Your Rights

Depending on your location, you may have rights to:
- Access, correct, or delete your personal data.
- Object to or restrict processing.
- Port your data (where applicable).
To exercise these rights, contact us at **EMAIL@YOURDOMAIN.COM**. We will respond according to applicable law.

---

## 7. Children’s Privacy

The App is **not** intended for children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe we have collected information from a child, contact us to request deletion.

---

## 8. Security

We take reasonable administrative and technical measures to protect information. However, no method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure — we cannot guarantee absolute security.

---

## 9. International Transfers

The App and our services may transfer and process data in countries different from yours. We will take steps required by law to ensure that transfers are secure.

